From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] SH2 dynarec: fast paths for work RAM, delay loops, a block cache

- The JIT's memory calls go to small handlers that read cached work RAM
  directly and write cached high work RAM directly while no compiled
  code comes from it (the setDirty bitmap of 0002).
- A "dt Rn; bf <itself>" delay loop runs in one step for the cycles
  left in the time slice (Virtua Fighter 2's slave SH2 polls the master
  with one: 62 % of its blocks).
- The dispatcher keeps the last blocks run by PC, with their flags, in
  a small direct-mapped cache: it found each block in a 4 MB table and
  read its flags 4 KB past its code, two cache misses per block. Every
  table entry is cleared through kill(), which drops the cached one.

Upstream-Status: Pending
